 "storyArc": "At a long dinner Hernando tells his best anecdote: the day in 1983 when Rosa threw a bucket of mop water over a senator who refused to pay. Then, without the jokes, he tells the other story: he had loved Rosa for forty years and never told her. Tomás learns that Joaquín left after Rosa refused to sell the building to pay his debts."
